      "stop_reason": "end_turn",
      "tool_uses": [],
      "assistant_text": "The Hub keeps the Anthropic API key out of its own process environment through **credential scoping**, as described in [[credential-scoping]]:\n\nThe key mechanism is that **a local secrets loader reads the key from a git-ignored \u0060.env\u0060 file at startup and injects it only into the environment of the spawned child process** (either the Ingest agent or Query agent), immediately before that process starts. Critically, the Hub\u0027s own process environment is never mutated to hold the key.\n\nThis design ensures that if the Hub process itself is compromised or misbehaves, it cannot leak the credential by inspecting its own environment variables \u2014 the key exists only inside the short-lived child process that actually needs to call the Anthropic API. The child processes receive the credential the same way, injected into their environments at spawn time, never inherited from or written into the Hub\u0027s environment.",
      "input_tokens": 5314,
      "output_tokens": 193
    }
